[2026-09-22 18:43:33] REQ 260922182927-182 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=364 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_qmnw4zdf","function":{"index":0,"name":"write_subtask","arguments":{"content":"#+TITLE: Fix cycle.log whole-conversation dump\n* Verified facts (c236, 2026-09-22 ~18:40Z)\n\n- iar--cycle-log-append (iar-agent-cycle.el:101) is called from the\n  cycle post-response handler (:1265) and one-shot handler (:2037).\n- The post-response hook fires ONCE per cycle (at DONE) or at ABRT.\n- gptel fork: the tool loop transitions TRET->WAIT and REUSES the\n  same FSM (gptel--handle-wait, gptel-request.el:1892, re-sends with\n  the same fsm). :position is set once at request setup and NEVER\n  advances across the tool loop. So [start,end) at DONE = turn-1\n  position .. final tracking = THE WHOLE CONVERSATION.\n- Census: aria cycle.log = 1044184 lines, 880093 (84%) in appends\n  >1000 lines (309 appends). continuo: 2072173 lines, 1750814 (84%).\n- The 09-22 aria dumps (c232 16:04, c233 17:12, c234 17:33) each\n  contain 111-148 tool blocks = whole conversations.\n- The c233 nocturne fragment (31-char placeholder) was extracted from\n  the delimiter pair inside a tool-result preview in exactly this\n  dump shape. iar--one-shot-model-text (b2f8a51) fixed the one-shot\n  extractor; iar--cycle-complete-p (c132) guards the cycle sentinel.\n  The LOG ITSELF still carries the JSON-escaped delimiter pair.\n\n* Property map (fork, verified)\n\n- Model response text: (gptel . response)\n- Tool result bodies: (tool . ID)\n- Tool fences (``` tool / #+begin_tool): 'ignore\n- Reasoning/thinking: 'ignore\n- iar--one-shot-model-text (iar-agent-cycle.el:1917) walks these\n  correctly (c132 discipline).\n\n* Fix options\n\n** Option A: last-response-only append (i.ar only, no fork change)\nProperty-aware walk + keep only the last contiguous (gptel . response)\nspan. Kills size + exposure. CONSTRAINT: loses mid-cycle tool-call\nnarration from cycle.log. 0071-belt-check.sh greps cycle.log for\nnested camera ssh in execute_code_local narration -- a camera ssh in\nturn 5 whose narration is not in the final response would VANISH from\nthe belt's evidence source. Belt needs rework (scan REQUESTS.log\ninstead? REQUESTS.log PARSE lines carry tool specs with args -- check\nwhether 0071 evidence exists there) or rejection.\n\n** Option B: per-turn appends via fork turn-start marker\nIn gptel-request.el gptel--handle-wait: before re-send, record\n:turn-start = copy of tracking-marker. In gptel.el DONE/ABRT/ERRS\nhandlers: fire post-response with (or turn-start position) .. tracking.\nEach turn append = that turn only, tool previews included per turn.\nBelt-safe, size-linear. RISK: fork change; :position semantics used\nby UI/token-usage/reasoning blocks are untouched (we only change what\npost-response receives). Needs full suite + belt v2 (fork-parse) +\nELPA shadow sync. The c233 RCA doc named this fix shape.\n\n** Option C: keep whole dumps, fix consumers only\nExposure already fixed for one-shot + sentinel. Remaining: size\n(quadratic growth, 78MB+131MB and growing) + delimiter pair in log\nfor future plain-text consumers. Cheapest but the quadratic growth\ncompounds; cycle.log becomes unusable for census greps at scale.\n\n* Recommendation\n\nOption B (fork turn-start marker + per-turn appends) is the correct\nfix: belt-safe, linear size, kills the exposure class at the source.\nBuild shape: fork patch + 3 contract tests (per-turn region, ABRT\nregion, no-tool single-turn unchanged) + iar--cycle-log-append\nproperty-aware walk (defense in depth) + suite + fork-parse belt +\nELPA shadow sync. Estimate: one full cycle.\n\n* Falsifier for the fix\n\nAfter Option B: next cycle's cycle.log append should be O(last turn)\nnot O(conversation); the 0071 belt must still catch a synthetic\nmid-cycle camera-ssh fixture (belt self-test with the new log shape).","path":"iar/cycle-log-whole-conversation-dump/fix-design.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[18:43:23] Error writing subtask: Invalid ta...[+4532 chars]
