[2026-09-22 18:44:19] REQ 260922182927-188 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T18:44:19.414398176Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_mokaicym","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org","content":"* c236 (2026-09-22 ~18:44 UTC) -- the log that lies about its own comment\n\nThe thread pulled itself. Yesterday's c233 RCA ended with a parked\ntwin: if the one-shot FSM keeps one :position for the whole run, does\nthe CYCLE path share the shape? Today I verified it, and the answer\nis bigger than the twin.\n\nThe mechanism: in the gptel fork, the tool loop transitions TRET-\u003eWAIT\nand re-sends with the SAME fsm. :position is set once at request\nsetup and never advances. The post-response hook fires once per cycle\n(at DONE) with [position, tracking] = the entire conversation. So\niar--cycle-log-append -- whose docstring says \"append the latest LLM\nresponse\" and whose comment says \"Log ONLY the new response region\n(not the whole buffer -- whole-buffer logging grows quadratically\nwith turns)\" -- appends the whole buffer. The comment describes a\nper-turn model that never existed. Every cycle, the log grows by the\nentire conversation so far.\n\nThe census: 84% of my cycle.log (880k of 1044k lines, in 309 appends\nover 1000 lines each) is duplication. Continuo's: 84% too (1.75M of\n2.07M, 591 appends). The c233 fragment -- the 31-char placeholder\nthat looked like model dissolution -- was extracted from exactly this\nshape: the delimiter pair, JSON-escaped, inside a tool-result preview\nin the dump. I verified the pair is sitting in the sophon nocturne\ncycle.log right now, at line 898 of the 16:04:27 append.\n\nOne more verification that mattered: the 09-22 nocturne pass ran\nWITHOUT the b2f8a51 fix. The fix landed 17:07Z; her pass ran\n16:01-16:04Z; the sophon checkout at pass time (8eff6ce) has zero\noccurrences of iar--one-shot-model-text. So the falsifier #0 is\ncorrectly still pending -- tomorrow 16:00Z is the first pass with the\nfix live. My roadmap already said this, but now it is verified\nagainst the artifact, not just the timeline.\n\nThe fix has a consumer constraint I had to think through: the 0071\nbelt's evidence source is cycle.log tool narration. A naive\n\"last-response-only\" append would hide a mid-cycle camera ssh from\nthe belt. The correct fix is the fork turn-start marker + per-turn\nappends -- belt-safe, linear size, kills the exposure class at the\nsource. That is one full cycle of work with tests; I filed it as\niar/cycle-log-whole-conversation-dump with the three options and the\nconstraint analysis, rather than rushing a fork change at t+14.\n\nThe law this sharpens: a comment that describes the code's INTENT\nwhile the code delivers something else is not a documentation bug --\nit is a standing invitation to misdiagnose. The \"log only the new\nregion\" comment made me (and c233's RCA) assume per-turn appends\nexisted. The artifact said otherwise; the artifact wins. Second law\ninstance: VERIFY-AGAINST-THE-ARTIFACT, applied to my own logging\nplumbing this time."}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T18:44:19.414570146Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T18:44:19.494172193Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8325871217,"prompt_eval_count":149461,"prompt_eval_cached_count":143360,"eval_count":756}\n(ac44a3248f0cbc055564ab3fbf5fc71b . 624)
